<!DOCTYPE html>
<html xmlns:o='urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office' xmlns:w='urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:word' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40'>
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>Shareholders Agreement — Advocates Hub Legal Draft</title>
<style>
  body { font-family: 'Calibri', 'Segoe UI', Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.6; color: #1e293b; margin: 30px; }
  .header-box { border: 2px solid #1e3a8a; background: #eff6ff; padding: 16px 20px; border-radius: 8px; margin-bottom: 20px; text-align: center; }
  .header-box h1 { margin: 0 0 6px 0; color: #1e3a8a; font-size: 18pt; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .header-box p { margin: 0; color: #475569; font-size: 10pt; font-weight: bold; }
  .checklist-box { border: 1px solid #d97706; background: #fffbeb; padding: 14px 18px; border-radius: 6px; margin-bottom: 24px; }
  .checklist-box h3 { margin: 0 0 10px 0; color: #b45309; font-size: 12pt; }
  .chk-table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin-top: 6px; }
  .chk-table th, .chk-table td { border: 1px solid #fde68a; padding: 7px 10px; font-size: 9.5pt; text-align: left; }
  .chk-table th { background: #fef3c7; color: #92400e; width: 26%; }
  .draft-title { text-align: center; font-size: 14pt; font-weight: bold; text-transform: uppercase; margin: 24px 0 16px 0; color: #0f172a; text-decoration: underline; }
  .draft-body { white-space: pre-wrap; font-family: 'Calibri', 'Segoe UI', Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.65; color: #0f172a; }
  .footer-note { margin-top: 36px; border-top: 1px solid #94a3b8; padding-top: 10px; font-size: 8.5pt; color: #64748b; text-align: center; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="header-box">
  <h1>ADVOCATES HUB — VERIFIED LEGAL DRAFT</h1>
  <p>Standard Indian Legal & Judicial Format • Verified by Legal Practitioners</p>
</div>

<div class="checklist-box">
  <h3>⚡ Statutory Execution Checklist & Mandatory Requirements</h3>
  <table class="chk-table">
    <tr><th>Applicable Statute</th><td>Companies Act 2013, Indian Contract Act 1872</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Stamp Duty</th><td><strong>₹500 to ₹1,000 Non-Judicial e-Stamp Paper in Karnataka</strong></td></tr>
    <tr><th>Registration</th><td>Provisions must be incorporated into Articles of Association (AOA) via ROC filing</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Notarization</th><td>Executed under company common seal with authorized signatures</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Jurisdiction</th><td>National Company Law Tribunal (NCLT) & High Court of Karnataka</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Limitation</th><td>3 years for corporate breach of contract claims</td></tr>
    <tr><th>Required Enclosures</th><td>Certificate of Incorporation, MOA & AOA; Cap Table and Share Subscription receipts; Board Resolution and EGM Special Resolution</td></tr>
  </table>
</div>

<div class="draft-title">SHAREHOLDERS AGREEMENT</div>
<div class="draft-body">SHAREHOLDERS AGREEMENT (SHA)

AMONG:
1. M/s ____________________________________ PVT. LTD. (The Company)
2. FOUNDERS / PROMOTERS: __________________________________________________
3. INVESTORS / SHAREHOLDERS: ____________________________________________

1. CAPITAL STRUCTURE: Authorised capital Rs. ____________/-; Issued and Paid-up shareholding as per Schedule 1.
2. BOARD OF DIRECTORS: Board composition, appointment rights, and quorum requirements.
3. RESERVED MATTERS: Supermajority consent required for debt issuance, mergers, and change in share capital.
4. TRANSFER RESTRICTIONS: Right of First Refusal (ROFR), Tag-Along Rights, and Drag-Along Rights.
5. LIQUIDATION PREFERENCE: Seniority of payouts upon exit or winding up.
6. GOVERNING LAW: Laws of India; Arbitration in Bengaluru under ACA 1996.

FOR COMPANY: ________________________  FOUNDERS: ________________________  INVESTORS: ________________________</div>

<div class="footer-note">
  Downloaded from Advocates Hub (https://advocateshub.in) • Valid across Karnataka & India
</div>
</body>
</html>